  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;All new works and works of making good to the retained fabric, whether internal or external, shall be finished to match the original work with regard to the methods used and to material, dimensions, composition, form, colour, finish and profile unless otherwise specified in the details hereby approved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reason: In order to protect the special interest of the listed building.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;A sample panel of brickwork for the replacement section of wall shall be prepared on site and approved in writing by the LPA prior to the commencement of the relevant part of the works. The panel shall accurately reflect the proposed brick, brick bond, mortar mix, pointing style and joint profile. The panel shall be retained on site until works are complete. The work shall be carried out in accordance with the details so approved, and shall be maintained as such thereafter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reason: In order to protect the special interest of the listed building and/or the character and appearance of the conservation area&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>"
  ],
